銃の管理人 (Jū no Kanri-nin): "Gun custodian" or "firearms caretaker."

Game written and art created by:
  Peter Keller (psilord@disaffectedhuman.com)
  Ryan Burnside (pixeloutlaw@gmail.com)

A shmup where you are inexplicably the very last ship that can save the world.

Milestones:

- [DONE] Create level-0 png data, 240 x 3600 for one 320 high screen in 8
  seconds for a total of 1 minute and 30 seconds of gameplay before boss is
  reached. Add scaffold that slides along the level with camera hanging from
  it. Use simple plane primitive to show position of the player.

  - Built from simple define-prefab.
  - Built scaffold.
  - Used ortho camera.
  - use direction-mover to move scaffold at right speed and stop at end.
 
- [DONE] Lift sprite system, render layer components, and get a non-moving
  player ship rendering with animated exhaust.

  - Added these components:
    - tags
    - delayed-render
    - sketch

- [DONE] Construct movement components for player, left stick and dpad support,
  non-rotating player. Support dpad and analog stick.

  - Added these components:
    - input-handler (disambiguates gamepads for now)
    - player-mover

- [DONE] Add projectiles used for bullets, etc. (physics layers,
  colliders, etc). Add a single bullet emitter that's good enough to use for
  a while.

  - Added these components:
    - projectile
    - emitter-split-arc
    - gun

    Currently, no damage can be taken or inflicted.

- [DONE] Add non-moving, non-rotating, non-shooting enemies into the world.

  - Simple prefab work.

- Give players/enemies/bullets the concept of damage points and hit points.
  Add in colliders (and the protocol APIs to the referents) as needed.

  - Added these components:
    - damage-points
    - hit-points
    - explosion

  Fixate which actors are on which physics layers.

- Enemy movement, autonomous steering behavior, waypoints and paths, etc.

  Sprite orientation code. Enemy shooting code.

  - Added these components
    - sprite-orienter (pick the right N, NE, S, SE, etc sprite)
    - enemy-mover (or a collection for different kinds of movement).

- Design all the player/enemy weapons and their spreads.

- Add enemy spawn points in level that spawn in the right circumstance.

  - Added these components:

- Add bitmap font, player score, maquettes for num players left, hang this
  stuff under the scaffold.

- Add director and reifiy state changes in game: splash screen, level-0 start,
  spawning, warning banner, boss behavior, dying, game over, you win.

